MEMORANDUM
TO:

Mayor Patrick Collins, and City Council
FROM:

TJ Barttelbort, Purchasing Manager
DATE:

May 7, 2024
SUBJECT:
Consideration of Bid #S-10-24 for an Agreement between the City of Cheyenne and
Reiman Corp., for the Hawk Signals Construction for Western Hills Blvd. & Moccasin
Ave. / Pershing Blvd. & McCann Ave. Project
______________________________________________
Bid #S-20-24 was solicited for the Hawk Signals Construction for Western Hills Blvd. & Moccasin
Ave. / Pershing Blvd. & McCann Ave. project (Project Vicinity Map included).

Two (2) bidders responded to this bid, and the bid tabulation is attached.  The Bids were received
from:
1. JTL Group Inc. d/b/a Knife River
2. Reiman Corp.

The bids were reviewed by Rick Amen (Engineering), Sam Berta (Engineering), and Tom Cobb
(Engineering) and their recommendation is to accept the lowest responsive bid from Reiman Corp.

The total Bid Award for the Base Bid is $755,722.50.  The City included a 10% Incentive if the
Contractor reaches Substantial Completion prior to August 22, 2024.  The 10% Incentive totals
$75,572.25.  Grand total for Base Bid & 10% Incentive is $831,294.75.

Project Completion is scheduled for October 31, 2024, or August 22, 2024 (If Incentive Date is met).

Funding:
025-21-2111-45-46515 (Transportation Alternatives Program (TAP) / Federal Grant)
$542,940.00
020-26-2617-42-43506 (1% Sales Tax 19-22 / Traffic and Safety Improvements)
$284,256.60
011-21-2111-42-86300, Proj# 53101 (FORMAK Grant Match HAWK Systems)
$4,098.15
```

